; TITHE - THE EMBER CHOIR, option 1: KINDLING
;
; Fire, and a choir that feeds it. D harmonic minor - the C-sharp is the
; heat - so its dominant, A, is the phrygian-dominant chord with a B-flat
; leaning on it. The harp is a FLAME: an arpeggio in 16ths that never stops,
; which is also what keeps a long planning phase moving. The choir sings over
; it in long notes and runs; war drums and a crackle of hat underneath.
; A falls from A to the tonic; B rises through the A chord to B-flat above.

song emberkindle "Ember Choir: Kindling"
groove 3
unit 16
rows 32
measure 16
states 3
voice lead choir
voice bass bass
voice chord harp

; --- the flame catches ----------------------------------------------------------
lead LI = o4 d4. e8 f4. e8 | c+4 d4 e2 |
bass BI = o2 l8 d d d d d d d d | a a a a a a a a |
chord HDA = o3 l16 d f a >d< a f d f d f a >d< a f d f |
            c+ e a >c+< a e c+ e c+ e a >c+< a e c+ e |
drum DI = k4 r4 k4 r4 | k8 t16 t16 t8 h8 k8 t8 s8 h8 |

; --- A: from A down to D ----------------------------------------------------------
lead LA1 = o4 a4. g8 f8 e8 f8 g8 | b-2 f4 d4 |
lead LA2 = o4 g4. f8 e8 d8 e8 f8 | e2 c+4 e4 |
lead LA3 = o4 a4. g8 f8 e8 f8 a8 | >d2 f4 d4< |
lead LA4 = o4 b-4 g4 a4 c+4 | d2. r4 |
; --- B: through A, up to B-flat ----------------------------------------------------
lead LB1 = o5 e4. f8 e8 d8 c+8 d8 | f2 e4 d4 |
lead LB2 = o5 e4. f8 e8 d8 c+8 <b-8 | a2. r4> |
lead LB3 = o5 d4 f4 b-4 a4 | g4 f4 e4 d4 |
lead LB4 = o5 c+4 d4 e4 c+4 | d2. r4 |

; --- THE BATTLE STATES (TITHE-PLAN 13.4): the flame, the bass and the drums do
; not change - only the lead and its instrument, at a pattern boundary.
; PRESSED: the choir is down to ONE VOICE, the chant - broken phrases, a
; breath before each, every line leaning a semitone into the note it wants
; (B-flat onto A, F onto E, and E-flat, the phrygian second, onto D).
; ASCENDANT: the SHAWM, a war reed - running eighths through the harmonic
; minor with its C-sharp, climbing to the D and F an octave above.
lead PI = @chant o4 d4 r8 d8 e-4 d4 | c+4 d4 e2 |
lead PA1 = @chant o4 a4 r8 a8 b-4 a4 | b-2 a4 r4 |
lead PA2 = @chant o4 g4 r8 g8 a4 g4 | e4 f4 e4 r4 |
lead PA3 = @chant o4 a4 r8 a8 b-4 a4 | f4 e4 d4 r4 |
lead PA4 = @chant o4 b-4 a4 c+4 e4 | d2. r4 |
lead PB1 = @chant o4 e4 r8 e8 f4 e4 | f4 e4 d4 r4 |
lead PB2 = @chant o4 e4 r8 e8 f4 e4 | d2 c+4 r4 |
lead PB3 = @chant o4 d4 r8 d8 e-4 d4 | d4 c4 <b-4 a4> |
lead PB4 = @chant o4 c+4 r8 c+8 d4 c+4 | d2. r4 |

lead XI = @shawm o5 d8 e8 f8 g8 a4 f4 | e8 f8 e8 d8 c+4 e4 |
lead XA1 = @shawm o5 a8. g16 f8 e8 f8 g8 a8 >d8< | b-4. a8 f4 d4 |
lead XA2 = @shawm o5 g8. f16 e8 d8 e8 f8 g8 b-8 | a4. g8 e4 c+4 |
lead XA3 = @shawm o5 a8. g16 f8 e8 f8 g8 a8 >c+8 | d4. c+8 d4 f4< |
lead XA4 = @shawm o5 b-8 a8 g8 b-8 a8 c+8 e8 g8 | f8 e8 d8 c+8 d4 r4 |
lead XB1 = @shawm o5 e8 f8 g8 f8 e8 d8 c+8 d8 | f8 g8 a8 g8 f8 e8 d4 |
lead XB2 = @shawm o5 e8 f8 g8 f8 e8 d8 c+8 <b-8 | a4. >d8 d4 r4 |
lead XB3 = @shawm o5 d8 f8 b-8 >d8 c8< b-8 a8 b-8 | g8 a8 b-8 a8 g8 f8 e8 d8 |
lead XB4 = @shawm o5 c+8 d8 e8 f8 e8 d8 c+8 e8 | d4 a4 >d4< r4 |

bass BDB = o2 l8 d d d d d d d d | <b- b- b- b- b- b- b- b-> |
bass BGA = o2 l8 g g g g g g g g | a a a a a a a a |
bass BGAD = o2 l8 g g g g a a a a | d d d d d d d d |
bass BAD = o2 l8 a a a a a a a a | d d d d d d d d |
bass BBG = o2 l8 <b- b- b- b- b- b- b- b-> | g g g g g g g g |

chord HDB = o3 l16 d f a >d< a f d f d f a >d< a f d f |
            d f b- >d< b- f d f d f b- >d< b- f d f |
chord HGA = o3 l16 d g b- >d< b- g d g d g b- >d< b- g d g |
            c+ e a >c+< a e c+ e c+ e a >c+< a e c+ e |
chord HGAD = o3 l16 d g b- >d< b- g d g c+ e a >c+< a e c+ e |
             d f a >d< a f d f d f a >d< a f d f |
chord HAD = o3 l16 c+ e a >c+< a e c+ e c+ e a >c+< a e c+ e |
            d f a >d< a f d f d f a >d< a f d f |
chord HBG = o3 l16 d f b- >d< b- f d f d f b- >d< b- f d f |
            d g b- >d< b- g d g d g b- >d< b- g d g |

drum DW = k8 t16 t16 t8 h8 k8 t8 s8 h8 | k8 t16 t16 t8 h8 k8 t8 s8 h8 |
drum DF = k8 t16 t16 t8 h8 k8 t8 s8 h8 | k8 t16 t16 t8 h8 s16 s16 s16 s16 T8 T8 |

order LI/PI/XI BI HDA DI
order LA1/PA1/XA1 BDB HDB DW          ; 1: the loop comes back here
order LA2/PA2/XA2 BGA HGA DW
order LA3/PA3/XA3 BDB HDB DW
order LA4/PA4/XA4 BGAD HGAD DF
order LB1/PB1/XB1 BAD HAD DW
order LB2/PB2/XB2 BAD HAD DW
order LB3/PB3/XB3 BBG HBG DW
order LB4/PB4/XB4 BAD HAD DF
loop 1
